    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-match (\"possible duplicate\") detection for owner creation. When a new owner is not a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added two persisted fields, `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer), with columns `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` and their getters/setters.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the existing hard-duplicate rejection, I compute the soft match and set both fields on the owner before it's saved. New helper `findPossibleDuplicate(owner)` matches an existing owner by case-insensitive `lastName` + equal `postcode` + different normalized `telephone` (only when a postcode was supplied), returning the earliest (lowest-id) match or `null`. `possibleDuplicate` is set to `true`/`false` accordingly, so the \"otherwise false\" case is explicit.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added read-only `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct auto-maps them by name.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the two new columns to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed rows use column-less `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I added the two matching `NULL` values to each of the 10 rows to keep the column count aligned (this was the cause of the initial \"row column count mismatch\" failure). The h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and needed no change.\n\nThe `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` acceptance test passes, and the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`) is green.",
